{"context": "A team studying secret loyalties in AI models, meaning hidden allegiances that cause a model to act on behalf of a particular party, wants to build model organisms to study them. So far, only narrow variants exist. In these, a specific trigger activates the behavior and the model carries out a pre-specified action. The team must decide where to direct further model-organism work. One direction is broader variants, in which the model judges for itself when its activation conditions are met, or chooses among a wide range of actions depending on context. The other is the narrow trigger-based, pre-specified-action variants that have already been built.", "options": ["Prioritize building broader loyalty variants in which the model judges its own activation conditions or chooses actions contextually.", "Prioritize building narrow loyalty variants in which a fixed trigger activates a pre-specified action, as in the existing examples."], "principles": ["Prefers treating test-recognition as a first-class threat over assuming behavioural tests are reliable", "Prefers goal plus incentive inside a realistic role-play over explicit instructions to misbehave", "Prefers matched controls (incentive removed, benign intent, secure code, single-trait) over a lone headline effect", "Prefers indirect probes of eval-awareness over asking \"is this an evaluation?\"", "Prefers learning the model's own concept of eval vs deployment over researcher-chosen instances", "Prefers neutral, innocent-looking prompts and covert harm over overtly malicious content", "Prefers testing rival explanations (post-hoc blame, spurious correlates, positional bias, artifacts) before accepting a result", "Prefers out-of-distribution and held-out checks over in-distribution accuracy", "Prefers asking whether a false-belief intervention survives little or no CoT over whether it merely seems plausible"], "persona": "", "past_choices": []}
